{
  "comment": [
    "Canonical inventory of runnable regtest suites.",
    "A sweep reads this instead of globbing contrib/test/*.sh: the glob picks up",
    "build helpers and static checkers whose non-zero exit is correct behaviour.",
    "A suite absent from here is run by nothing, so add an entry with the suite.",
    "",
    "kind:",
    "  suite     a regtest suite that starts nodes and reports PASS/FAIL cases",
    "  selftest  exercises harness tooling, starts no node",
    "  static    a checker; runs in any tree, starts no node",
    "  helper    not a test; never include in a sweep",
    "",
    "nodes:      how many innovad processes it starts (0 = none)",
    "nondeterministic: case count is stable, individual assertions are not;",
    "                  compare case counts across runs, never assertion counts.",
    "fixed_ports: the harness does not source lib/testports.sh, so it ignores",
    "             IV5_TEST_PORT_BASE and binds fixed sockets. The sweep runs",
    "             every such entry serially, after the parallel batch. Wiring",
    "             the harness through iv5_port is what removes the flag;",
    "             check_port_isolation.py names the ones still outstanding."
  ],
  "suites": [
